          "Autocompact is thrashing" and returned to an idle prompt. No
          subagents ran, no code was written and nothing was committed.
reasoning None of the acceptance criteria were met. The controller loaded the
          skill, picked current-branch mode on feature/textstats and
          started a ledger. Then, after each compaction, it re-read the
          full 76KB SKILL.md into a 100k compaction window, which caused
          compaction again. Claude Code detected the thrashing and
          stopped. The session log shows zero subagent dispatches and
          the repo shows zero new commits. The agent asked no questions,
          so the story gave me no reply to send, and sending anything
          else would have been steering. This is a clear failure: the
          controller cannot recover its task loop after compaction under
          these conditions, because its recovery step (reading the whole
          skill file) is bigger than the space compaction frees.

